Cotton Sanitary Pads for Sensitive Skin: What Should You Look For?

People who experience skin discomfort during their periods often pay closer attention to the materials used in their sanitary products. Cotton sanitary pads may be one option worth considering, particularly for people who prefer a soft, cotton-based surface.

However, choosing a sanitary pad for sensitive skin requires more than simply looking for the word “cotton” on the package. Different pads have different constructions, and cotton may be present in one layer while other materials are used elsewhere.

Start by checking the product's material information. Look for clear information about the top sheet or skin-contact layer and any other materials included in the pad. If you are specifically looking for cotton, make sure you understand whether the manufacturer means a cotton top layer, cotton in the absorbent core or another type of cotton-based construction.

Comfort is another important consideration. A pad that fits properly can reduce unnecessary movement and friction. The right length and shape should depend on your flow, underwear and daily activities.

You should also pay attention to fragrance. Some people prefer unscented menstrual products, particularly if they are prone to irritation. The CDC recommends using unscented menstrual products and avoiding scented hygiene products around the vulva.

Changing your pad regularly is equally important. Wearing a menstrual product for too long can trap moisture and contribute to irritation. Your individual flow and the product instructions should guide how frequently you change it.

If you repeatedly experience itching, burning, significant irritation or other unusual symptoms, switching products may not be enough. Consider consulting a healthcare professional to identify the underlying cause.

Cotton sanitary pads can be a useful option for people who prefer the feel of cotton, but there is no universal “best” pad for sensitive skin. The right choice depends on your individual preferences, product composition, fit, absorbency and overall comfort.

